The manifest's >0.75 coefficient-error diagnostic trigger fired in several low-information datasets. Investigation showed that every MLE had higher likelihood than its generating parameter vector; the same generated bytes gave matching R/Julia fitted likelihoods and matching generating-parameter likelihoods to numerical precision. All four fits converged and had finite gradients below 1e-4. The trigger is documented, not treated as a recovery pass. Two datasets per cell do not establish recovery, bias, coverage, or calibration.
